How much Plant Avaibale Water(PAW, in length in.) is in the root zone of the Hyalite soil series? There is 3.2in of PAW associated with 31.1in of soil which with some quick math, informs us that there is 83%PAW relative to the total thickness of the soil. This very high PAW could be off due to the fact that the CDM/Welsh traignles estimates FC and PWP based on texture without taking into account two very important factors being rocks and Soil Organic Matter(SOM). As far as we understand rock does not absorb much water compared to SOM which acts as a sponge compared by ignoring these factors the PAW will be severly over estimated since it assumed the soil is fine when it is infact very cobbly. 
